<title>FRANCE: CYCLING-DUNKIRK FOUR DAYS SIXTH STAGE PLACINGS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-DUNKIRK FOUR DAYS SIXTH STAGE PLACINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LE MONT-NOIR, France 1997-05-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading placings in</p>
<p>the Dunkirk Four Days cycling race after the sixth stage on</p>
<p>Saturday:</p>
<p> 1. Daniele Contrini (Italy) Brescialat  four hours 25 minutes</p>
<p>27 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Franck Vandenbroucke (Belgium) Mapei</p>
<p> 3. Andrei Tchmil (Ukraine) Lotto		    all same time</p>
<p> 4. Christophe Mengin (France) Francaise des Jeux    2 seconds</p>
<p>behind</p>
<p> 5. Vladimir Melli (Italy) Brescialat</p>
<p> 6. Johan Musseuw (Belgium) Mapei		   both same time</p>
<p> 7. Philippe Gaumont (France) Gan one minute 42 seconds behind</p>
<p> 8. Laurent Roux (France) TVM</p>
<p> 9. Cedric Vasseur (France) Gan</p>
<p> 10. Mariano Piccoli (Italy) Brescialat	    all same time</p>
<p>Overall standings:</p>
<p> 1. Museeuw			   10 hours 43 minutes 35 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Vandenbroucke				    11 seconds behind</p>
<p> 3. Contrini						    27 seconds</p>
<p> 4. Tchmil								  29</p>
<p> 5. Mengin								1:11</p>
<p> 6. Vladimir Belli (Italy) Brescialat			   1:27</p>
<p> 7. Nico Mattan (Belgium) Mapei				   2:07</p>
<p> 8. Leon van Bon (Netherlands) Rabobank			 2:13</p>
<p> 9. Arturas Kasputis (Lithuania) Casino			 2:24</p>
<p> 10. Michelangelo Cauz (Italy) Aki				2:36</p>
</text>
